  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South Carolina received $8.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. South Carolina logged 16,223 awards with an average award size of $520K, and obligations were up 1.3% year over year. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in the state, obligating $4.8B, followed by the Department of Defense at $2B. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC and SAVANNAH RIVER MISSION COMPLETION, LLC are the top two vendors, receiving $3.4B and $1.1B respectively. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $3.6B, with Remediation Services next at $1.1B. Annual obligations have varied: FY21 totaled $6.7B, FY22 totaled $7.2B, FY23 totaled $10.1B, FY24 totaled $10.6B, FY25 totaled $8.3B, and FY26 stands at $8.4B so far. This profile shows a concentration of obligations in energy and environmental services, significant single-vendor awards, and steady award activity through the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are federal obligations in South Carolina?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy leads buying with $4.8B in obligations. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC received $3.4B and SAVANNAH RIVER MISSION COMPLETION, LLC received $1.1B. Facilities Support Services accounts for $3.6B of obligations, highlighting large contracts in facility and remediation work."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has federal spending in South Carolina trended recently?",
        "body": "FY26 obligations sit at $8.4B to date, higher than FY25 obligations of $8.3B and lower than FY24 obligations of $10.6B. Obligations rose year over year by 1.3%. Award volume and size remain substantial with 16,223 awards and an average award size of $520K."
      }
    ]
  },
